            {
                "entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                "word": "bergerie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3d2fb539-57f9-4ae6-a3fc-6f9dead1b22e",
                        "entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bergeries"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "128bb88d-81c3-3c1a-9faf-953d7428e940",
                        "entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lieu où l’on enferme un troupeau de moutons, de brebis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a034ab5-6df7-433c-a80f-eba924e36212",
                                "sense_id": "128bb88d-81c3-3c1a-9faf-953d7428e940",
                                "text": "Sous le ciel pâlissant, les bâtiments de la Borderie sommeillaient encore, à demi sombres, trois longs bâtiments aux trois bords de la vaste cour carrée, la bergerie au fond, les granges à droite, la vacherie, l’écurie et la maison d’habitation à gauche."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed882f0b-aaae-4b63-9426-15e58158a081",
                                "sense_id": "128bb88d-81c3-3c1a-9faf-953d7428e940",
                                "text": "La bergerie était longue, la grange était haute."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa1c7189-5acf-43ab-abfb-ac96cbf7f135",
                                "sense_id": "128bb88d-81c3-3c1a-9faf-953d7428e940",
                                "text": "D’où le surnom de Jonah Lomu des bergeries, en référence au mythique rugbyman des All Blacks."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73b398ec-f818-35f9-99f1-05868ea12482",
                        "entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Poème ou récit bucolique mettant en scène les amours des bergers et des bergères."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "097b906b-e88d-4d99-bf60-f178240153df",
                                "sense_id": "73b398ec-f818-35f9-99f1-05868ea12482",
                                "text": "[L’auteur] a laissé railler ses bergeries comme il avait laissé railler tout le reste, sans s’inquiéter des arrêts de certaine critique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f145a29-817a-4c3f-8a2f-89ae95ac6ec5",
                                "sense_id": "73b398ec-f818-35f9-99f1-05868ea12482",
                                "text": "Au point où l’Île-de-France, le Valois et la Picardie se rencontrent, —divisés par l’Oise et l’Aisne, au cours si lent et si paisible, il est permis de rêver les plus belles bergeries du monde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6b3a6f3-9a43-4349-aafe-0777511ceef4",
                                "sense_id": "73b398ec-f818-35f9-99f1-05868ea12482",
                                "text": "Et, rêveuse, câline, elle revenait à ses bergeries, à ses petits sentiers de verdure, au calme de l’existence douce et cachée, avec des fleurs, des bêtes, et de l’amour…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f616b3d4-e185-47b5-bbe3-218ffed9a550",
                        "source_entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "target_lang_word": "Schafstall",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Schafstall",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22dfdfef-2af7-38fe-b52c-cdff3ca6c662",
                                        "entry_id": "4a480e84-67e0-3ccd-b1fb-eeede9122f46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gebäude, das der Unterbringung von Schafen dient"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45b66259-5051-4f97-a9b1-f1048aa7bdef",
                                                "sense_id": "22dfdfef-2af7-38fe-b52c-cdff3ca6c662",
                                                "text": "Die Schafe verkrochen sich im Schafstall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08c5446a-e29b-4052-9a11-eca59f67d0bc",
                                                "sense_id": "22dfdfef-2af7-38fe-b52c-cdff3ca6c662",
                                                "text": "„Unweit des Hauses standen Schafställe, aber die eingezäunte Fläche stand leer.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92ec7a4d-a73f-492b-82e2-c491fae0de7a",
                                                "sense_id": "22dfdfef-2af7-38fe-b52c-cdff3ca6c662",
                                                "text": "„Es kam gar nicht so selten vor, dass ich im Winter nur in den Schafstall gegangen bin, um ihnen beim Wiederkäuen und Stöhnen zuzuhören und dem Rütteln des Windes am Wellblech.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69b870f6-96d3-4444-8510-50e05449d9b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "target_lang_word": "sheepfold",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sheepfold",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78d51184-717d-3f56-b54a-eb3a1dd649e7",
                                        "entry_id": "b9170d56-0901-30c4-a73b-9e2fe58b11eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An enclosure for keeping sheep."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eae0d02a-e79e-4cb3-b5c3-0ebbf48dd6f6",
                                                "sense_id": "78d51184-717d-3f56-b54a-eb3a1dd649e7",
                                                "text": "If civilized life had covered over the ancient verities, Dumuzi learns in his tragic death that the sheepfold is still there to reclaim him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "904024ad-3ea7-3f5f-9c1a-dcee6d2fb245",
                                        "entry_id": "b9170d56-0901-30c4-a73b-9e2fe58b11eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A flock of sheep."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "41e6dcfc-c96f-47b7-a620-a84423aeec7c",
                        "source_entry_id": "96ca4752-1274-31fc-b80e-626b86209998",
                        "target_lang_word": "sheepcote",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sheepcote",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2a6951a-0d41-33ee-ae74-41916fee77b1",
                                        "entry_id": "9c58fe9e-86f1-3ace-90a1-93ee1ac17a88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small building for sheltering sheep."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "731da31e-85f9-4191-964a-2989552a6919",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a6951a-0d41-33ee-ae74-41916fee77b1",
                                                "text": "If thou wilt come and dwell with me at home, My sheepcote shall be strowed with new greene rushes: Weele haunt the trembling prickets as they rome About the fields, along the hauthorne bushes; I have a pie-bald curre to hunt the hare, So we will live with daintie forrest fare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74901ed9-7a12-4158-afc7-56848e31d0a9",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a6951a-0d41-33ee-ae74-41916fee77b1",
                                                "text": "Each officer was at his post, nor could they much complain whilst their General sat on straw, in a sheepcote, at the foot of the hill, called Sherriff Muir, which overlooks Dumblane, on the right of his army."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0845886-5cc1-4eb3-8435-e32c268c4c93",
                                                "sense_id": "f2a6951a-0d41-33ee-ae74-41916fee77b1",
                                                "text": "Besides this, he acquired in the sheepcote lessons which he practised on the throne, that rule means service, and that the shepherd of men holds his office in order that he may protect and guide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
